.TH CCOL_ITER_NEXT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_iter_next \- move a unified iterator on to the next element
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/citerators.h>   /* or any container header */

cmap_iterator *ccol_iter_next(it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
ccol_iter_next moves the iterator to the next element by calling its
_next_fn callback. At the end of the sequence it destroys the iterator
and returns NULL. The argument is evaluated exactly once.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it   Iterator variable that ccol_iter_declare() declares, or an iterator
     inside ccol_for_each().
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The new value of the iterator, or NULL after the last element.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Once ccol_iter_next() has returned NULL the iterator is already
destroyed, so do not call ccol_iter_destroy() on it after that.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_begin (3),
.BR ccol_iter_declare (3),
.BR ccol_iter_destroy (3)
